@startuml sm2_in_progress
!include style.iuml
title SM-2  Game: IN_PROGRESS - sub-state diagram (UC-02, UC-03, UC-04)
hide empty description
state IN_PROGRESS {
  [*] --> BlackToMove : start()\n/ Black always moves first
  BlackToMove --> WhiteToMove : playTurn(row, col)\n[legal move and White has a valid move]
  WhiteToMove --> BlackToMove : playTurn(row, col)\n[legal move and Black has a valid move]
  BlackToMove --> BlackToMove : playTurn(row, col)\n[legal move and only Black has a valid move]\n/ White skipped
  WhiteToMove --> WhiteToMove : playTurn(row, col)\n[legal move and only White has a valid move]\n/ Black skipped
  BlackToMove --> BlackToMove : playTurn(row, col)\n[illegal move]\n/ InvalidMoveError, board unchanged
  WhiteToMove --> WhiteToMove : playTurn(row, col)\n[illegal move]\n/ InvalidMoveError, board unchanged
  BlackToMove --> [*] : playTurn(row, col)\n[neither player has a valid move]
  WhiteToMove --> [*] : playTurn(row, col)\n[neither player has a valid move]
}
IN_PROGRESS --> FINISHED : gameOver\n[neither player has a valid move]
IN_PROGRESS --> FINISHED : forfeit(color)\n[player quits or opponent gone > 30 s]
note bottom of IN_PROGRESS
  Each legal move runs Board.placePiece() -> Board.flipPieces()
  -> Piece.flip(), then GameService saves a MoveRecord.
  Against the computer, playComputerTurn() calls
  ComputerPlayer.makeMove(board) and then Game.playTurn().
end note
@enduml
